    3. Construct the full output on the tile lattice -- place 2-4 marker groups. For each group, pick a unique marker color and an eligible subcell. Place a straight H or V segment (2 markers) or an L-shape (3 markers sharing a corner). Ensure no (tile, subcell) conflicts and segment lengths >= 3.
    4. Build the output pixel grid: separator rows/cols, frame rings, base interiors, then paint marker segments.
    5. Derive input by keeping only the endpoint markers in each group; revert all intervening segment cells back to the base interior pattern value.
